NAME
    wc - count lines, words, and bytes

SYNOPSIS
    wc [FILE...]
    wc -l [FILE...]
    wc -w [FILE...]
    wc -c [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Counts lines, words, and bytes in each FILE (or stdin if none).
    Default output is "LINES WORDS BYTES FILENAME". With a single
    flag, only that count is emitted.

      -l    count lines (newline-terminated)
      -w    count words (whitespace-delimited)
      -c    count bytes

    A "word" is any maximal run of non-whitespace characters. A
    "line" is a string ending in a newline; the final unterminated
    line is still counted.

    --advjson mode (session 82) emits a single JSONL summary record
    per file: {"file": "...", "lines": N, "words": N, "bytes": N}.

EXAMPLES
    wc -l /etc/passwd                   # how many users
    cat *.txt | wc                      # totals across all .txt
    ls / | wc -l                        # how many entries

EXIT STATUS
    0   counts emitted
    1   I/O error
